{"book":10,"chapter":2,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / GETTING TO KNOW RUST / CHAPTER 2","slides":[{"title":"A variable and let","sub":"Chapter 2 · A name and a value","short":"Intro","main":"let binds a name to a value; three features: immutability, one type, shadowing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Name and value","Python","Rust"],"captions":["A variable is a name under which a program stores a value","In Python: x = 5 — a name can be bound to anything at any time","In Rust: let x = 5; — three features: immutable by default, one type forever, shadowing"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":44.0,"text":"x\n5","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"name → value","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["x = 5","x = \"hello\"   # allowed"],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["let x = 5;","// x = \"hello\";   error"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":280.0}]],"cues":[12.9,27.9]}]},{"title":"Immutability","sub":"A value is written once","short":"Immutable","main":"Without mut a variable cannot be changed; this protects against bugs.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["let x = 5","x = 6 ✕","Why"],"captions":["Without the word mut a variable is immutable: the value is written once","A second assignment is not allowed: error[E0384]: cannot assign twice to immutable variable","The reader sees the declaration and knows the value will not change — fewer bugs, especially with threads"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":44.0,"text":"x\n5","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"🔒 read-only","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let x = 5;","x = 6;"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"w":320.0,"h":30.0,"text":"error[E0384]: cannot assign twice to\nimmutable variable `x`","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"see let →\nvalue is constant","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fewer places\nto look for a bug","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[16.1,26.1]}]},{"title":"mut","sub":"Mutable variables","short":"mut","main":"let mut lets you change the value in place; += is a shortcut.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["let mut","+= operations","Warning"],"captions":["mut means “mutable”: now the value can be overwritten in place","x = x + 1; can be shortened to x += 1; likewise -=, *=, /=","If you declared mut but never changed it, the compiler warns: “variable does not need to be mutable”"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut x = 5;","x = 6;      // ok"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":300.0,"y":60.0,"w":56.0,"h":40.0,"text":"x\n6","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let mut n = 10;","n += 5;      // 15","n -= 3;      // 12","n *= 2;      // 24"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let mut y = 3;","println!(\"{y}\");"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"w":320.0,"h":28.0,"text":"warning: variable does not need to be mutable","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.7,27.1]}]},{"title":"Variable types","sub":"Inference and explicit form","short":"Types","main":"The type is inferred or written after a colon, and never changes.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Type inference","Explicit type","Type does not change"],"captions":["Types are inferred: 5 → i32, 2.5 → f64, \"hello\" → &str","A type can be written after a colon: let x: i64 = 5; — needed for a different number size","A variable's type does not change: you cannot store a string in x: i32 — mismatched types"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let a = 5;        // i32","let b = 2.5;      // f64","let c = \"hello\";  // &str"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let big: i64 = 5;","let small: u8 = 200;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let mut x = 5;","x = \"five\";"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"w":320.0,"h":28.0,"text":"error[E0308]: mismatched types: expected integer","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.6,30.4]}]},{"title":"Shadowing","sub":"let x = x + 1","short":"Shadowing","main":"A new variable covers the old one; the type can change.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["New variable","Old one covered","Type changes"],"captions":["let x = 5; let x = x + 1; — not a change, but a new variable with the same name","From here x means the new one: the old one is “shadowed” and no longer accessible","Shadowing can change the type: spaces → their count (a &str became a number)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let x = 5;","let x = x + 1;"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":160.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"x (old)\n5","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":98.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"x (new)\n6","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":250.0,"y1":58.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":82.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let x = 5;","let x = x + 1;","println!(\"{x}\");  // 6"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let spaces = \"   \";","let spaces = spaces.len();","// now the number 3"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"w":200.0,"h":22.0,"text":"&str  →  usize","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.7,24.1]}]},{"title":"mut or shadowing","sub":"Which to use","short":"Which one","main":"Accumulate — mut; transform — shadowing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["mut: same place","let: new value","Which to use"],"captions":["mut overwrites the value in place and keeps the type — for counters and accumulators","shadowing creates a new value and can change the type; the result can be made immutable","Transform — shadowing; accumulate a result — mut"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":60.0,"h":40.0,"text":"n\n1","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":130.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":66.0,"w":60.0,"h":40.0,"text":"n\n2","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":160.0,"y":40.0,"text":"n += 1","size":9.5,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"same cell","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":"s: &str\n\"42\"","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":190.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":66.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":"s: i32\n42","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"new cell, other type","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"transform → let","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"accumulate → mut","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.4,22.2]}]},{"title":"Scope","sub":"Blocks {}","short":"Blocks","main":"A variable lives until the closing brace of its block.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Block {…}","Shadowing inside","After the block"],"captions":["A block is any pair of curly braces: a variable lives from its declaration to the closing brace","Inside a block you can shadow an outer variable: while inside, the name means the new one","After leaving the block the name means the old variable again; the inner one is destroyed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let x = 1;","{","    let y = 2;   // y lives here","}","// y is not here"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let x = 1;","{","    let x = 100;   // new x","    println!(\"{x}\");  // 100","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let x = 1;","{ let x = 100; }","println!(\"{x}\");   // 1"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.8,21.6]}]},{"title":"Constants","sub":"const","short":"const","main":"const — computed at build time, type required, NAME IN CAPITALS.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["const","Name and type","const and let"],"captions":["const MAX: u32 = 100; — the value is known at compile time and substituted right into the code","The type is required; names are written in CAPITALS_WITH_UNDERSCORES; can be declared outside functions","const never changes, takes no stack space and is visible everywhere; let is a runtime variable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["const MAX: u32 = 100;","const SECONDS_IN_DAY: u32 = 24 * 60 * 60;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"SCREAMING_SNAKE","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"type required","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"const: at build time","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":50.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"let: at run time","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"const is never mut","size":10.0}]],"cues":[14.5,28.6]}]},{"title":"Deferred initialization","sub":"let x;","short":"No value","main":"You can assign later, but only once and before use.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["let x;","if branches","Cannot read"],"captions":["A variable can be declared without a value and assigned later — exactly once","Handy when a condition picks the value: one thing in one branch, another in the other","Reading a variable before assignment is not allowed: the compiler checks every execution path"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let x: i32;","x = 5;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let size;","if big {","    size = 100;","} else {","    size = 10;","}"],"hl":[2,4],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let x: i32;","println!(\"{x}\");"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"w":320.0,"h":28.0,"text":"error[E0381]: used binding `x` isn't initialized","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.5,25.9]}]},{"title":"Destructuring","sub":"let (a, b)","short":"Pairs","main":"let (a, b) = (1, 2); _ — value not needed; swap (a, b) = (b, a).","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A pair at a time","Underscore","Swap"],"captions":["let (a, b) = (1, 2); declares two variables in one expression","_ instead of a name means “value not needed”; a name starting with _unused silences the warning","(a, b) = (b, a); swaps the values without a temporary variable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let (a, b) = (1, 2);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":120.0,"y":110.0,"w":50.0,"h":36.0,"text":"a\n1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":240.0,"y":110.0,"w":50.0,"h":36.0,"text":"b\n2","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let (_, y) = (10, 20);","let _unused = 5;"],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["let mut a = 1;","let mut b = 2;","(a, b) = (b, a);   // a = 2, b = 1"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[11.5,25.9]}]},{"title":"Common mistakes","sub":"Reading messages","short":"Errors","main":"The compiler message usually already contains a help.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Assignment","Extra mut","Types and emptiness"],"captions":["“cannot assign twice to immutable variable” — add mut if the value really must change","“variable does not need to be mutable” — remove mut","“mismatched types” — a number and a string in one variable; “used binding isn't initialized” — a value might not have been set"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":300.0,"h":34.0,"text":"E0384: cannot assign twice","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":300.0,"h":28.0,"text":"help: let mut x = 5;","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":300.0,"h":34.0,"text":"warning: unused mut","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":300.0,"h":28.0,"text":"help: remove this `mut`","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":300.0,"h":28.0,"text":"E0308: mismatched types","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":80.0,"w":300.0,"h":28.0,"text":"E0381: isn't initialized","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"the error text already has a hint","tone":"green","size":9.5}]],"cues":[12.5,21.8]}]},{"title":"After Python","sub":"What changed","short":"After Python","main":"mut — same value; let — new one; global and nonlocal are not needed.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Python","Rust: two paths","No global"],"captions":["In Python a name can be bound to anything at any time: a number, then a string, then a list","In Rust: same value, same type — mut; a new value or type — shadowing with let","global and nonlocal are not needed: there are exactly as many scopes as there are {} blocks"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["x = 5","x = \"five\"","x = [5]"],"lang":"rust","size":13.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"mut: change\n(same type)","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"let: new one\n(any type)","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":240.0,"h":34.0,"text":"block {…} = scope","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.8,19.1]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next — data types.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["let — immutable; let mut — mutable (same type); let again — shadowing; const — a constant with a type","Scope is a block; you can declare without a value and assign once; (a, b) unpacks a pair","Next chapter — data types: integers, floats, booleans and characters"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"let","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"let mut","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shadowing","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"const","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let a = 1;","let mut b = 2;","b += a;","let b = b * 10;","const C: u8 = 7;"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"i32","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"f64","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"bool","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"char","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.9,21.0]}]}]}